 "title": "Protein-Protein Interactions and Cellular Processes Involving SLC26A4 and ZBTB16",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the interactions between SLC26A4 and ZBTB16, two proteins that are co-expressed in human cells. SLC26A4 interacts with CUL3 and ROC1, and is ubiquitinated by ubiquitin. ZBTB16 interacts with multiple proteins, including CUL3, ROC1, and SLC26A4. The cluster also includes other proteins involved in cellular processes, such as Gcn2, eIF2α, and Hsf1, which regulate protein synthesis and stress responses. The interactions between these proteins suggest complex regulatory mechanisms in human cells.",
